{{Quote|Presenting His Excellency, Mok Shaiz, Mayor of Mos Espa and its surrounding plateaus.|[[8D8]]|<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}}</ref>}}
'''Mok Shaiz''' was an [[Ithorian]] [[Gender|male]] who was the [[Mayor of Mos Espa|mayor]] of the [[city]] of [[Mos Espa]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] in [[9 ABY]]. Following [[Boba Fett]]'s [[Fett gotra|takeover]] of the [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]] and [[Jabba's criminal empire|criminal empire]] of [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba the Hutt]], Shaiz and Fett came into conflict after the latter failed to pay him tribute, instead having expected the [[Mayor]] to do the same to him. When Fett was subsequently attacked in an [[Ambush outside of the Sanctuary|assassination attempt]], the new [[crime lord]] visited Shaiz, believing he was responsible, though the Mayor deflected both the accusation and the threats made by Fett. In reality, Shaiz had offered Fett's territory on Tatooine to the [[Pyke Syndicate]]. He was [[Assassination of the Pyke Syndicate leaders|killed]] by [[Master Assassin]] [[Fennec Shand]] while in hiding with the other [[Crime lord|crime bosses]] of Mos Espa.

==Biography==
===The Mayor and the Daimyo===
{{Quote|Master Bib did not have the power of Jabba, so he relied on uneasy alliances to preserve his tribute and title. All of this while lining the pockets of Mayor Mok Shaiz.|[[8D8]]|<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" />}}
[[File:MayorsThrone-BOBFC2.png|thumb|right|300px|As the Mayor of Mos Espa, Mok Shaiz governed from a throne room within the city hall.]]
The [[Ithorian]] [[Gender|male]] Mok Shaiz governed as the [[Mayor of Mos Espa|mayor]] of the [[city]] [[Mos Espa]] and its surrounding plateaus on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]]. Shaiz resided in a [[Mos Espa City Hall|city hall]] within Mos Espa, where he was served by a [[Mok Shaiz's majordomo|Twi'lek majordomo]] and several guards, as well as a [[Unidentified clerk|desk clerk]]. He took visitors' appointments from within his chambers in the city hall.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

After the [[death]] of the [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba the Hutt]]<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" /> in [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> his [[majordomo]], [[Bib Fortuna]],<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" /> took his place amid the newly-created power vacuum. Mos Espa subsequently became divided between three families&mdash;the [[Strassi family|Trandoshans]], the [[Aqualish crime family|Aqualish]], and the [[Tatooine Klatooinian family|Klatooinians]]. As Fortuna possessed less power than Jabba had, he had to rely on uneasy alliances, providing Shaiz with payment.<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" />

In the [[Standard year|year]] [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> the former [[bounty hunter]] [[Boba Fett]], assisted by [[Master Assassin]] [[Fennec Shand]], [[Attack on Jabba's Palace (Boba Fett)|killed]] Fortuna, taking over his [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]].<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> Unknown to Fett, Shaiz had been bribed by the [[Pyke Syndicate]],<ref name="The Gathering Storm">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}}</ref> who the Mayor promised the territory that Fett had claimed.<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" /> As Fett tried to rebuild the [[Hutt]]'s [[Jabba's criminal empire|criminal empire]] as [[Fett gotra|his own]], receiving tributes from many of those who formerly served under Jabba, Shaiz dispatched his majordomo to Fett's palace. Though Fett and Shand believed Shaiz himself would be visiting to pay tribute, the majordomo only offered his employer's welcome, informing the new [[Daimyo]] that the Mayor was occupied with pressing matters and instead requesting that Fett pay tribute to Shaiz. Fett did not provide any tribute for the Mayor, but allowed the majordomo to depart alive. Before leaving, the majordomo informed the two that Shaiz may take Fett's response differently, threatening the possibility of a further delegation in the near future.<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" />

===Assassination accusation===
{{Quote|You should remember, you serve as long as the Daimyo of Tatooine deem it so.''"<br />"''Before you threaten me, you should ask yourself, who really sent the Night Wind? I have no motive. As you said, I serve at your pleasure.''"<br />"''I am not a fool, Mok Shaiz. And those who thought otherwise no longer draw breath.|Boba Fett and Mok Shaiz|<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />}}
After Fett and Shand were [[Ambush outside of the Sanctuary|attacked]] by [[assassin]]s<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> of the [[Order of the Night Wind]], they captured [[Unidentified Night Wind assassin|one]], who alleged that he had been sent by the Mayor. Fett and Shand subsequently took the [[prisoner]] to the city hall, and the majordomo attempted to turn them away, claiming Shaiz was indisposed for the remainder of the [[Standard week|week]]. Fett nonetheless forced his way into the Mayor's quarters as the majordomo apologized to Shaiz.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

[[File:FettMayorMeeting-BOBFC2.png|thumb|left|300px|Boba Fett confronted Shaiz after an assassination attempt that he believed had been orchestrated by the Mayor.]]
The Mayor questioned the identity of the unannounced visitor, though Fett was doubtful that the Ithorian did not know who he was. Fett threw the Night Wind assassin to the ground in front of Shaiz, accusing the Mayor of being behind the attack. The majordomo insisted that the Mayor was not responsible, but Shaiz silenced him, identifying the assassin's allegiance to the Night Wind. Though Fett took the Mayor's comment as admission, Shaiz silently signaled one of his guards, who shot and killed the assassin; the act led to a standoff between Fett's forces and the Mayor's guards, but Shaiz continued with acknowledgment of the Night Wind's illegal nature outside [[Hutt Space]], thanking Fett for turning the assassin in.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

As the majordomo rewarded Fett at the Mayor's request, Fett declared he was no longer a [[bounty]] [[Hunting|hunter]], but Shaiz challenged his claim. Fett asserted that he would take the payment in place of the tribute he had expected from Shaiz, threatening that the Mayor only served as the Daimyo deemed. Shaiz, unfazed by the threat, suggested that Fett reconsider who was behind the Night Wind attack, claiming that he had no motive and that he served at Fett's pleasure, though the crime lord was unconvinced. Offering advice to Fett as his tribute, along with the currency provided earlier, Shaiz told him that running a family was a more complicated endeavor than bounty hunting; when Fett questioned him, the Mayor instructed the Daimyo to visit Madam [[Garsa Fwip]]'s [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|Sanctuary]], where Fett learned that his position was disputed by the Hutts known as [[the Twins]], a [[Unidentified Hutt brother|brother]] and [[Unidentified Hutt sister|sister]] who were cousins of Jabba.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

===Truth revealed===
{{Quote|Where is he?''"<br />"''He's with the Pykes. The Mayor's gone. He's working with the Pykes.|Boba Fett and Shaiz's majordomo|<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" />}}
[[File:Majordomocaptive.png|thumb|right|300px|The Twi'lek majordomo claimed the mayor was on a planned vacation.]]
Some time later, the Twins learned that Shaiz had promised Tatooine to the Pyke Syndicate, informing Fett, who was doubtful of their claims. The crime lord attempted to confront the Mayor in the city hall, but Shaiz had already departed to join the [[Pyke]]s,<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" /> who had begun to gather their [[troop]]s<ref name="The Gathering Storm" /> in Mos Espa. After Fett, helped by a gang of [[Mods]], chased down Shaiz's majordomo when he attempted to flee the city hall, the majordomo told him that Shaiz had gone.<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" /> The Mayor's majordomo was captured and questioned by Fett and Shand, but Shaiz himself could not be found, though the Mods were dispatched to search the streets of Mos Espa for him.<ref name="The Gathering Storm" /> Eventually, following the Pyke Syndicate expansion on Tatooine, the majordomo believed Shaiz had fled offworld. The Twi'lek claimed that it was a scheduled vacation.<ref name="From the Desert Comes a Stranger">{{BOBF|Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger}}</ref>

===Hiding and death===
{{Quote|No more explosives. I didn't sign off on bombing Garsa's sanctuary. I agreed to surgical strikes, not open warfare.|Mok Shaiz|<ref name="In the Name of Honor">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>}}
In truth, the mayor had gone into hiding with the Pykes in [[Mos Eisley]], holing up in the [[Desert Survey Office]]. Shaiz was conversing with the [[Pyke Boss|Pyke boss]] in charge of the Syndicate's Tatooinian operations when the [[Duros]] [[Cad Bane]] reported in on the state [[Freetown]]'s involvement. Shaiz questioned whether the [[Tusken Raider]] [[Unidentified Tusken Raider tribe|tribe]] Fett was accepted into would be a problem, leading the Pyke boss to confess that the Syndicate arranged their massacre and framed it on a [[Nikto]] [[Kintan Striders Gang|biker gang]]. At the revelation, Shaiz expressed his frustration with the complicating events, citing the [[Destruction of Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|bombing]] of the [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|Sanctuary]] earlier in the night, and reiterated he had only agreed to "surgical strikes" that wouldn't leave his city destroyed.<ref name="In the Name of Honor" />

[[File:MokShaizDead-BoBFCh7.png|thumb|left|300px|Shaiz was hanged by Fennec Shand, killed alongside his fellow conspirators.]]
Following the Syndicate's defeat at the [[Battle of Mos Espa]], Shaiz was sat with the dons of the Mos Espa crime families as the Pyke boss announced their withdrawal from Tatooine due to the inhospitality for their [[spice]] trade. Shaiz began to argue that Tatooine was hospitable, only for the Pyke to shut him up by rhetorically asking if half of his men getting shot or eaten by a [[Boba's rancor|rancor]] was what he considered "hospitable." Shaiz paused along with the room's occupants when they heard the sound of two gunshots from outside, and stood up when everyone else drew their weapons in defense. Within a span of seconds, sniper fire came in through the windows, killing the three dons and the pair of [[Pyke sentinel]]s. Shaiz began hyperventilating, looking for a way out, when a loop of cable fed down from the ceiling and slipped around the base of his neck. The Ithorian fought to pull at the thin noose, but the cable winched up, strangulating him until his neck broke. Shaiz's body hung limply in the middle of the office, leaving the cornered Pyke officiate frantically firing through the ceiling of a room littered with six corpses.<ref name="In the Name of Honor" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Here is the tribute I offer, some advice. Running a family is more complicated than bounty hunting.|Mok Shaiz, to Boba Fett|<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />}}
[[File:Mok_Shaiz_Ithorian_Databank.png|thumb|right|250px|Shaiz was conniving, yet cowardly.]]
Though Mok Shaiz hid his true affiliation,<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" /> he asserted that he had no motive against Fett, claiming to Fett that he served at the crime lord's pleasure,<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" /> while the Mayor's majordomo greeted Boba Fett with what he said was Shaiz's heartfelt welcome. Nevertheless, the Mayor expected the crime lord to pay him tribute rather than the opposite,<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> also acting as if he was unaware of Fett's identity when they met. When Fett brought the captured Night Wind assassin to Shaiz along with an accusation, the Mayor instead responded as if Fett was still operating as a bounty hunter.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" /> The Mayor was referred to as "spineless" by one of the Twins.<ref name="The Streets of Mos Espa" />

Mok Shaiz had [[Color|dark green]] [[eye]]s and pale skin.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

==Skills and abilities==
As an Ithorian, Mok Shaiz spoke the [[Ithorese]] [[language]].<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

==Equipment==
Mok Shaiz made use of a [[translator collar]] that translated his Ithorese speech into [[Galactic Basic Standard|Galactic Basic]]. The Mayor wore a long green [[Clothing|garment]] that was adorned with gold.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:MayorMeetingConcept-BOBFC2.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Concept art of Mok Shaiz and Boba Fett by Anton Grandert.]]
Mok Shaiz is a character that was created for the television series ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]''. Shaiz was portrayed by performance artist [[John Rosengrant]]<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" /> and was one of two characters voiced by co-showrunner and director [[Robert Rodriguez]],<ref name="THR">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-features/robert-rodriguez-interview-book-of-boba-fett-star-wars-1235062364|text=How 'The Book of Boba Fett' Will Shake Up 'Star Wars'|author=Hibberd, James|date=2021-12-16|archivedate=20211216143038}}</ref> alongside [[Dokk Strassi]].<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> He first featured in the series' trailer on [[November 1]], [[2021]]<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|rOJ1cw6mohw|The Book of Boba Fett &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/official-trailer-the-book-of-boba-fett}}</ref> and was later mentioned by name in the first episode of the series, "[[Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land]],"<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> which aired on [[Disney+]] on [[December 29]], 2021.<ref name="D23 E1">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-december-2021|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in December 2021}}</ref> Shaiz first appeared in the following episode, "[[Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine]],"<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" /> which aired on [[January 5]], [[2022]].<ref name="D23 E2">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-january-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in January 2022}}</ref>

Concept art of Shaiz's meeting with Fett in Chapter 2 was created by [[Anton Grandert]].<ref name="C2 Concept">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1480222949521035265|[[Star Wars]]|quote=Check out some of the official concept art from Chapter Two of #TheBookOfBobaFett. Art by Anton Grandert (2/4)|archivedate=20220109170101}}</ref> The Mayor's depiction in the concept art differs slightly from his final appearance, featuring different clothing and sporting a beard.<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

